

->  What is JVM?
JVM (Java Virtual Machine) is a virtual machine that:
Runs Java bytecode (.class)
Makes Java platform independent
Manages memory, threads, and garbage collection


-> Main Components of JVM
    ClassLoader Subsystem
    Runtime Data Areas
        Heap
        Stack
        Method Area
        PC Register
        Native Method Stack
    Execution Engine
    Garbage Collector
    JNI (Java Native Interface)


-> Role of Execution Engine
Execution Engine:
Executes bytecode line by line
Uses:
Interpreter → Executes bytecode one instruction at a time
JIT Compiler → Converts bytecode to machine code for speed
Works with Garbage Collector
📌 Without Execution Engine, Java code cannot run.





